WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.240
The Lucy Show Starring Lucille Ball

00:08.240 --> 00:32.240
Co-Starring Vivian Vance

00:32.240 --> 00:55.240
Co-Starring Lucy

00:55.240 --> 00:58.240
Lucy, is Chris out of the bathroom yet?

00:58.240 --> 01:00.240
No.

01:00.240 --> 01:02.240
I don't want to get dressed.

01:02.240 --> 01:05.240
I've got to take a shower.

01:05.240 --> 01:11.240
Do you think she's ever coming out of there?

01:11.240 --> 01:18.240
I certainly hope so, because I have to wash off this beauty mask before it gets hard.

01:18.240 --> 01:20.240
Chris is always monopolizing the bathroom.

01:20.240 --> 01:22.240
What takes her so long in there?

01:22.240 --> 01:24.240
Oh, you know how teenagers are.

01:24.240 --> 01:26.240
They're not washing their hair.

01:26.240 --> 01:29.240
They're rolling it up or taking it down or trying out a new style.

01:29.240 --> 01:30.240
Yeah.

01:30.240 --> 01:35.240
Or brushing it or spraying it or washing out the spray.

01:35.240 --> 01:39.240
Or rolling it up again.

01:39.240 --> 01:44.240
You think she'd come out of there once in a while just to use the rest.

01:44.240 --> 01:48.240
Well, one good thing, while she's in the bathroom, at least she's not tying up the phone.

01:48.240 --> 01:52.240
Oh, can you imagine what would happen if we had a telephone in there?

01:52.240 --> 01:53.240
Good heavens.

01:53.240 --> 01:57.240
I wouldn't see Chris until she was old enough to vote.

01:57.240 --> 01:59.240
Chris!

01:59.240 --> 02:02.240
I'd better get out in the kitchen and wash this off.

02:02.240 --> 02:03.240
Yeah.

02:03.240 --> 02:07.240
Chris, are you ever coming out of there?

02:07.240 --> 02:12.240
Well, what are you two doing?

02:12.240 --> 02:14.240
Is that you, Aunt Lucy?

02:14.240 --> 02:17.240
Yes, it's me, Aunt Lucy.

02:17.240 --> 02:20.240
This is a facial mask I'm wearing to make me look pretty.

02:20.240 --> 02:25.240
Gee, Mom, I bet you'd look prettier without it.

02:25.240 --> 02:30.240
Well, thank you, honey.

02:30.240 --> 02:33.240
What's come over you two, washing in the middle of the day?

02:33.240 --> 02:35.240
We're going to the wash.

02:35.240 --> 02:36.240
So?

02:36.240 --> 02:40.240
They sloughed my filth.

02:40.240 --> 02:42.240
Well, I see somebody beat you to the annex.

02:42.240 --> 02:44.240
Yeah, I'm afraid so.

02:44.240 --> 02:48.240
Lucy, do you think it would do any good if I called Chris' boyfriend and had him call her,

02:48.240 --> 02:56.240
and while they're talking on the telephone I could rush into the bathroom and stake out a claim in the name of the great unwashed?

02:56.240 --> 02:58.240
No, I'm afraid not.

02:58.240 --> 03:00.240
Mom, we're going to the Y to play basketball.

03:00.240 --> 03:02.240
Okay, darling.

03:02.240 --> 03:04.240
Okay, Jerry, here you are.

03:04.240 --> 03:07.240
Now, remember, be sure and take a shower before you come home.

03:07.240 --> 03:08.240
We have to?

03:08.240 --> 03:09.240
Yes, you have to.

03:09.240 --> 03:12.240
We do, frown on filth.

03:12.240 --> 03:13.240
Bye.

03:13.240 --> 03:16.240
Take a shower for me.

03:16.240 --> 03:20.240
You know, Viv, one bathroom is just not enough for five people.

03:20.240 --> 03:21.240
Of course it isn't.

03:21.240 --> 03:22.240
It never has been.

03:22.240 --> 03:25.240
I'm just going to have to install a second bathroom.

03:25.240 --> 03:27.240
Oh, now, Lucy, we've been over all of that before.

03:27.240 --> 03:29.240
You just can't afford it.

03:29.240 --> 03:32.240
Well, there's just one thing that we're going to have to do.

03:32.240 --> 03:37.240
You and the boys and I are going to have to come out every morning, jump in the car, put the top down,

03:37.240 --> 03:42.240
ride in the Danfield, and go through the car wash.

03:42.240 --> 03:45.240
That's a thought.

03:45.240 --> 03:50.240
Hey, you know, I could just put in a shower instead of a whole bathroom.

03:50.240 --> 03:51.240
That way it wouldn't cost so much.

03:51.240 --> 03:55.240
Yeah, but Paisley the plumber would still charge you plenty for the labor.

03:55.240 --> 03:56.240
Well, I'm going to call him.

03:56.240 --> 03:58.240
Maybe he's having a sale.

03:58.240 --> 03:59.240
Maybe so.

03:59.240 --> 04:01.240
You know, we wouldn't even have to tear down a wall.

04:01.240 --> 04:04.240
We could put the shower in that closet in the boys' room.

04:04.240 --> 04:06.240
Hey, you better wash off that facial mask.

04:06.240 --> 04:07.240
Why?

04:07.240 --> 04:11.240
Because in just a few minutes you're going to be ready for Mount Rushmore.

04:11.240 --> 04:16.240
Now don't use all the hot water in the wash.

04:16.240 --> 04:18.240
What?

04:18.240 --> 04:22.240
That much to install a shower?

04:22.240 --> 04:27.240
Mr. Paisley, if you don't lower your prices, you're liable to bring on socialized plumbing.

04:27.240 --> 04:30.240
I'm going to say to you too, Mr. Paisley.

04:30.240 --> 04:31.240
What'd he say?

04:31.240 --> 04:33.240
Just what you said he would say.

04:33.240 --> 04:35.240
Boy, these prices.

04:35.240 --> 04:40.240
Apparently the only way to get clean is to be filthy rich.

04:40.240 --> 04:47.240
Hey, you know, if I bought the equipment and had a friend install the shower, it wouldn't cost half as much.

04:47.240 --> 04:53.240
If the friend you have in mind is who I think it is, that friend thinks you're out of your mind.

04:53.240 --> 04:56.240
Viv, I wouldn't ask you to do a thing like that.

04:56.240 --> 04:57.240
Thanks.

04:57.240 --> 05:01.240
You don't know anything about plumbing.

05:01.240 --> 05:02.240
Who did you have in mind?

05:02.240 --> 05:04.240
Good old Harry next door.

05:04.240 --> 05:07.240
Oh, now, Lucy, we can't ask Harry to do anything else for us.

05:07.240 --> 05:09.240
We're always imposing on him.

05:09.240 --> 05:10.240
That's not imposing.

05:10.240 --> 05:12.240
Harry enjoys doing things for us.

05:12.240 --> 05:15.240
It feeds his ego.

05:15.240 --> 05:20.240
It seems to me that by now his ego would be as fat as a horse.

05:20.240 --> 05:22.240
Well, where are you going?

05:22.240 --> 05:23.240
Over to Harry's.

05:23.240 --> 05:28.240
The sooner he starts on the shower, the sooner we'll have it.

05:28.240 --> 05:30.240
Oh, Harry, hi.

05:30.240 --> 05:31.240
I'm sorry.

05:31.240 --> 05:32.240
It's all right.

05:32.240 --> 05:34.240
You just dented my bumper a little.

05:34.240 --> 05:36.240
Where are you going in such a rush?

05:36.240 --> 05:37.240
I was going over to see you.

05:37.240 --> 05:38.240
Forget it.

05:38.240 --> 05:39.240
I'm not there.

05:39.240 --> 05:45.240
That's funny.

05:45.240 --> 05:48.240
You're funny, Harry.

05:48.240 --> 05:49.240
What did you want to see me about?

05:49.240 --> 05:51.240
Oh, well, what did you come over here for?

05:51.240 --> 05:53.240
To invite your lovely girl for lunch.

05:53.240 --> 05:54.240
Oh, great.

05:54.240 --> 05:55.240
Come on, Lucy, let's get dressed.

05:55.240 --> 05:57.240
No, we can't go.

05:57.240 --> 05:59.240
Why not?

05:59.240 --> 06:01.240
Well, don't you remember, Viv?

06:01.240 --> 06:02.240
I was going over to Harry's.

06:02.240 --> 06:03.240
Don't you remember?

06:03.240 --> 06:05.240
I was going to invite him over here for lunch.

06:05.240 --> 06:06.240
You were?

06:06.240 --> 06:07.240
Yeah.

06:07.240 --> 06:08.240
Oh, yeah, yeah, she was.

06:08.240 --> 06:09.240
She was.

06:09.240 --> 06:10.240
That's right.

06:10.240 --> 06:13.240
Now you just sit down, Harry.

06:13.240 --> 06:14.240
Relax.

06:14.240 --> 06:19.240
Get nice and comfy, and I'm going to make you your favorite dish, eggs Benedict.

06:19.240 --> 06:20.240
Hold it.

06:20.240 --> 06:23.240
All right, Lucy, what do you want me to do?

06:23.240 --> 06:26.240
Whatever do you mean?

06:26.240 --> 06:33.240
I have learned from bitter experience that any time you offer me anything more than a peanut butter sandwich,

06:33.240 --> 06:41.240
you have something you either want repaired, shoveled, lifted, or taken out of a trap and buried.

06:41.240 --> 06:45.240
Well, that just shows you how wrong you can be, Harry.

06:45.240 --> 06:49.240
Oh, Harry, you have such a suspicious nature.

06:49.240 --> 06:51.240
You mean you just want me to have lunch?

06:51.240 --> 06:53.240
I don't have to do anything?

06:53.240 --> 06:54.240
Not a thing.

06:54.240 --> 06:55.240
Oh, thanks.

06:55.240 --> 07:00.240
Unless, of course, you'd like to show your appreciation by installing an extra shower for me.

07:00.240 --> 07:03.240
Ha, ha, I knew it.

07:03.240 --> 07:05.240
Install a shower.

07:05.240 --> 07:06.240
That's a big job.

07:06.240 --> 07:09.240
Well, Harry, I don't mean for you to do it now while I'm fixing your lunch.

07:09.240 --> 07:11.240
I mean do it next weekend.

07:11.240 --> 07:14.240
Couldn't I just have a peanut butter sandwich?

07:14.240 --> 07:16.240
Harry, it's a snap.

07:16.240 --> 07:17.240
Come on, Lucy.

07:17.240 --> 07:19.240
I'm no plumbing expert.

07:19.240 --> 07:21.240
Oh, you're so modest.

07:21.240 --> 07:24.240
You know, you're a whiz at fixing soft-up sinks.

07:24.240 --> 07:28.240
Well, that's a lot different than installing a whole shower.

07:28.240 --> 07:30.240
I can't do that by myself.

07:30.240 --> 07:32.240
Oh, well, you'll have help.

07:32.240 --> 07:33.240
Yeah, who?

07:33.240 --> 07:36.240
Well, um, come in.

07:36.240 --> 07:37.240
Hi, Cussie.

07:37.240 --> 07:38.240
Hi, Eddie.

07:38.240 --> 07:39.240
Eddie.

07:39.240 --> 07:40.240
Hi, Lucy.

07:40.240 --> 07:43.240
Hey, we were just talking about you.

07:43.240 --> 07:44.240
You were?

07:44.240 --> 07:47.240
Yeah, how would you like some eggs Benedict?

07:47.240 --> 07:50.240
Yeah, how would you like some eggs Benedict?

07:50.240 --> 07:51.240
Oh, that'd be wonderful.

07:51.240 --> 07:53.240
Just marvelous.

07:53.240 --> 07:58.240
Oh, yeah.

07:58.240 --> 08:07.240
I'm coming outside.

08:07.240 --> 08:08.240
Hi, Harry.

08:08.240 --> 08:09.240
Hi, Ed.

08:09.240 --> 08:10.240
I want you to meet Joe Melvin.

08:10.240 --> 08:11.240
This is Harry Connors.

08:11.240 --> 08:12.240
How are you?

08:12.240 --> 08:13.240
Hello, Joe.

08:13.240 --> 08:15.240
Boy, am I glad to see you.

08:15.240 --> 08:19.240
I just discovered I don't know a snake from a plumber's friend.

08:19.240 --> 08:22.240
With me.

08:22.240 --> 08:23.240
Where are the girls?

08:23.240 --> 08:24.240
They're out shopping.

08:24.240 --> 08:25.240
Why?

08:25.240 --> 08:29.240
My boy, how would you like to get out of this whole ugly mess?

08:29.240 --> 08:31.240
Great, but how?

08:31.240 --> 08:32.240
I've got a plan.

08:32.240 --> 08:36.240
You see, Joe here is a plumber from Ridgebury.

08:36.240 --> 08:38.240
Buddy!

08:38.240 --> 08:44.240
Now, would you be willing to put out a little money to get out of installing that shower?

08:44.240 --> 08:46.240
Is it under a million dollars?

08:46.240 --> 08:48.240
I'll give you my rock bottom price.

08:48.240 --> 08:49.240
You got a deal.

08:49.240 --> 08:51.240
All right, my boy, I'll tell you what we're going to do.

08:51.240 --> 08:57.240
We're going to tell the girls that Joe here is an old friend of ours who will do the job for nothing.

08:57.240 --> 09:01.240
Then we split the bill, take the weekend off, and the girls don't know the difference.

09:01.240 --> 09:02.240
Is that good?

09:02.240 --> 09:03.240
Good.

09:03.240 --> 09:05.240
It's inspiring.

09:05.240 --> 09:07.240
Would you mind if I ask a question?

09:07.240 --> 09:08.240
Go ahead.

09:08.240 --> 09:10.240
Why don't you just tell the two ladies the truth?

09:10.240 --> 09:11.240
Because they'd never go for it.

09:11.240 --> 09:18.240
No, they don't mind us giving up our weekends or breaking our back, but they'd never allow us to pay you.

09:18.240 --> 09:20.240
After all, they've got their pride.

09:20.240 --> 09:21.240
Oh.

09:21.240 --> 09:23.240
Well, look, I'd better get to work.

09:23.240 --> 09:26.240
You guys started paying me the minute I walked through that door.

09:26.240 --> 09:28.240
I'll show you where the shower goes now.

09:28.240 --> 09:29.240
It's in the closet in the boys' room.

09:29.240 --> 09:34.240
Now, Harry, remember, we tell the girls that we meant to do the job with Joe,

09:34.240 --> 09:40.240
but suddenly you have to take a flight to Honolulu, and I've got a client in town from L.A.

09:40.240 --> 09:44.240
And then we stay out of their way for the entire weekend.

09:44.240 --> 09:45.240
You got it?

09:45.240 --> 09:47.240
Oh, I got to hand it to you, Eddie.

09:47.240 --> 09:52.240
I always knew you were clever, but you turned out to be positively crafty.

09:52.240 --> 09:55.240
Come on, come on, come on.

10:03.240 --> 10:05.240
Well, how's it going, Joe?

10:05.240 --> 10:07.240
It ought to be finished in an hour or two.

10:07.240 --> 10:08.240
Good.

10:08.240 --> 10:13.240
Gee, you must be a good friend of Eddie and Harry to let them take advantage of you like this.

10:13.240 --> 10:14.240
Huh?

10:14.240 --> 10:15.240
Oh, yeah, yeah.

10:15.240 --> 10:18.240
Do you know how much a real plumber would charge for this?

10:18.240 --> 10:20.240
How much?

10:20.240 --> 10:22.240
Oh, I hate to tell you.

10:22.240 --> 10:26.240
You know what robbers they all are.

10:26.240 --> 10:28.240
Now, just a minute.

10:28.240 --> 10:30.240
Some of my best friends are plumbers.

10:30.240 --> 10:31.240
Oh, wow.

10:31.240 --> 10:33.240
Of course, there are good ones and bad ones.

10:33.240 --> 10:34.240
Yeah.

10:37.240 --> 10:39.240
What do you do for a living, Joe?

10:39.240 --> 10:41.240
Well, I'm...

10:42.240 --> 10:44.240
What do you think I do?

10:44.240 --> 10:48.240
Well, from the looks of your sensitive hands,

10:48.240 --> 10:51.240
I'd say you were a doctor.

10:52.240 --> 10:53.240
You guessed it.

10:53.240 --> 10:55.240
I can always tell.

11:00.240 --> 11:02.240
Ma, can we watch Joe?

11:02.240 --> 11:04.240
Well, you can if you don't bother the man.

11:04.240 --> 11:05.240
We won't.

11:05.240 --> 11:06.240
All right, sit down there and be quiet now.

11:06.240 --> 11:09.240
He's very, very busy, so be quiet.

11:10.240 --> 11:12.240
Well, there it is, Jerry.

11:12.240 --> 11:15.240
A shower right in our room.

11:15.240 --> 11:18.240
We won't have any excuse for not washing again.

11:19.240 --> 11:22.240
That's one of the most depressing sights I have ever seen.

11:25.240 --> 11:27.240
Hey, Joe, where's the bathtub?

11:27.240 --> 11:28.240
Well, this is a stall shower.

11:28.240 --> 11:29.240
There's no tub.

11:30.240 --> 11:32.240
This is different from our other shower.

11:32.240 --> 11:36.240
Then I can get out of using this one on a technicality.

11:36.240 --> 11:37.240
How come?

11:37.240 --> 11:39.240
There's no place to set my boat.

11:39.240 --> 11:41.240
Joe, where does the water go off?

11:41.240 --> 11:42.240
Oh, right there.

11:45.240 --> 11:47.240
How come it's covered up?

11:47.240 --> 11:49.240
Well, you see, this is a test plug.

11:49.240 --> 11:51.240
It has to stay screwed on over the drain

11:51.240 --> 11:53.240
until the inspector okays it.

11:53.240 --> 11:54.240
Oh.

11:54.240 --> 11:55.240
What's an inspector?

11:55.240 --> 11:58.240
Now, now, now, I told you not to bother the man.

11:58.240 --> 11:59.240
Come on, downstairs.

11:59.240 --> 12:01.240
Why don't you go out and play or something?

12:04.240 --> 12:06.240
Well, how's it going, Joe?

12:06.240 --> 12:08.240
How's it going, Joe?

12:09.240 --> 12:10.240
Well, it would go a lot faster

12:10.240 --> 12:13.240
if you wouldn't keep coming in here every few minutes

12:13.240 --> 12:15.240
asking how's it going, Joe?

12:16.240 --> 12:18.240
Yeah, I suppose so.

12:24.240 --> 12:27.240
Joe, isn't that shower head a little low?

12:27.240 --> 12:29.240
It's the standard height.

12:29.240 --> 12:31.240
Well, it looks a little low to my eye.

12:31.240 --> 12:34.240
I think it should be about five inches higher.

12:34.240 --> 12:37.240
Look, it's too late to do anything about it now.

12:37.240 --> 12:38.240
It's already in.

12:38.240 --> 12:40.240
Yeah, and the way it is, Joe,

12:40.240 --> 12:43.240
that's a pretty sloppy caulking job.

12:43.240 --> 12:45.240
I'm not finished with it yet.

12:45.240 --> 12:47.240
Well, I suppose I shouldn't complain.

12:47.240 --> 12:49.240
After all, you are an amateur.

12:50.240 --> 12:52.240
Oh, nothing personal, Joe.

12:52.240 --> 12:56.240
Say, should you be using that wrench on that?

12:58.240 --> 13:00.240
Just what do you suggest I use?

13:00.240 --> 13:03.240
Well, I think you should use that doohickey right there.

13:03.240 --> 13:05.240
You're liable to borrow that hardware with that wrench.

13:05.240 --> 13:07.240
How would you like to do this yourself?

13:08.240 --> 13:10.240
Well, now let's not get huffy.

13:10.240 --> 13:12.240
I'm not getting huffy.

13:12.240 --> 13:16.240
Well, now for a doctor you have very good eyes.

13:16.240 --> 13:18.240
I'm not getting huffy.

13:18.240 --> 13:20.240
I'm not getting huffy.

13:20.240 --> 13:24.240
Well, now for a doctor you have very nasty bedside manners.

13:26.240 --> 13:31.240
What would you say if I told you I was a plumber?

13:32.240 --> 13:36.240
Well, if you are, you could fool the panel on what's my line.

13:38.240 --> 13:41.240
Well, it just so happens I am a plumber.

13:41.240 --> 13:42.240
You are not.

13:42.240 --> 13:45.240
You're a doctor friend of Eddie's and Harry's.

13:45.240 --> 13:47.240
I never saw them before in my life.

13:47.240 --> 13:53.240
And the only operation I ever performed was removing a spoon from a garbage disposal.

13:54.240 --> 13:56.240
If you're not a friend, why are you doing this?

13:56.240 --> 13:58.240
Because they're paying me.

13:58.240 --> 14:00.240
They're paying you?

14:01.240 --> 14:02.240
Where are you going?

14:02.240 --> 14:03.240
I'm quitting.

14:03.240 --> 14:05.240
If they're paying you, you can't quit.

14:05.240 --> 14:09.240
Lady, there isn't enough money in the world to get me to finish this job.

14:09.240 --> 14:10.240
Here.

14:11.240 --> 14:12.240
Wait a minute.

14:12.240 --> 14:14.240
What do you want me to do with this?

14:14.240 --> 14:17.240
Finish it yourself with a doohickey.

14:23.240 --> 14:25.240
What's he mumbling about?

14:25.240 --> 14:27.240
He just walked out on the job.

14:27.240 --> 14:30.240
Well, that's a fine thing for a friend of Eddie and Harry's to do.

14:30.240 --> 14:33.240
Friend? He isn't even a doctor.

14:34.240 --> 14:36.240
Who isn't even a friend or a doctor?

14:36.240 --> 14:39.240
I'll bet he isn't even a plumber.

14:39.240 --> 14:42.240
Who isn't even a friend or a doctor or a plumber?

14:42.240 --> 14:45.240
Why, wait till I get my hands on those two sneaks.

14:45.240 --> 14:47.240
What two sneaks?

14:47.240 --> 14:50.240
Lucy, will you please tell me what you're talking about?

14:50.240 --> 14:53.240
I'll tell you later, while we're finishing the shower.

14:54.240 --> 14:55.240
Wait a minute.

14:55.240 --> 14:58.240
What do you mean, while we are finishing the shower?

14:58.240 --> 14:59.240
Oh, it won't be hard.

14:59.240 --> 15:02.240
There's nothing much to do but hang the door and put in the faucet handles.

15:02.240 --> 15:04.240
He was almost finished.

15:04.240 --> 15:05.240
Who was almost finished?

15:05.240 --> 15:09.240
The friend, the doctor, the plumber, or one of the two sneaks?

15:09.240 --> 15:12.240
Go get on your working clothes and I'll tell you.

15:12.240 --> 15:17.240
Now, Lucy, I've helped you do a lot of things, but I draw the line at plumbing.

15:17.240 --> 15:24.240
Now, Viv, do you want to hear the story about the friend, the doctor, the plumber, and the two sneaks, or don't you?

15:24.240 --> 15:29.240
Oh, the things I do to bring a little drama into my life.

15:29.240 --> 15:31.240
Now, dress and hurry back.

15:37.240 --> 15:38.240
There.

15:38.240 --> 15:39.240
Now, that wasn't bad, was it?

15:39.240 --> 15:41.240
No, as a matter of fact, that was pretty simple.

15:41.240 --> 15:47.240
You know, I don't know why those two sneaks didn't do this themselves instead of throwing all that money away on that plumber.

15:47.240 --> 15:52.240
Well, I don't know why they didn't do it either, but I don't know why you're so mad at them for being willing to pay for it.

15:52.240 --> 15:54.240
You were willing to have them do it for free.

15:54.240 --> 15:58.240
Well, that's different. One's charity and one's friendship.

15:58.240 --> 16:03.240
Besides, do you realize if they hadn't spent all that money on Joe, they could have spent it on us?

16:03.240 --> 16:06.240
You're right. They are a couple of sneaks.

16:06.240 --> 16:09.240
Hey, you get out and turn on the water, man. We'll see how this works, huh?

16:09.240 --> 16:10.240
Yes, sir.

16:10.240 --> 16:13.240
Wait a minute. You better take this. I think it's going to be a little hard to turn.

16:13.240 --> 16:15.240
Oh, okay.

16:15.240 --> 16:35.240
Hurry up now.

16:35.240 --> 16:42.240
Turn it off! Turn off the water, man! Turn it off! We're leaking!

16:42.240 --> 16:44.240
Turn it off, man!

16:44.240 --> 16:45.240
What are you yelling about?

16:45.240 --> 16:47.240
Turn off the water! We're leaking!

16:47.240 --> 16:51.240
I can't turn it off. The panel broke off when I turned it off.

16:51.240 --> 16:53.240
Oh, well.

16:53.240 --> 16:55.240
What kind of fun was there making anyhow?

16:55.240 --> 16:59.240
Don't ask me. Are you sure you used the right washer?

16:59.240 --> 17:01.240
Washer?

17:01.240 --> 17:04.240
Yeah, those little round things.

17:04.240 --> 17:07.240
So that's what they were.

17:07.240 --> 17:10.240
Come on in here and help me turn off this water.

17:10.240 --> 17:11.240
Okay, what do I do?

17:11.240 --> 17:13.240
Well, come on in here. Get a hold of this one over here.

17:13.240 --> 17:14.240
Turn it off?

17:14.240 --> 17:17.240
Yeah, well, if we can't turn it off, tighten them up.

17:17.240 --> 17:21.240
Oh, wait a minute.

17:21.240 --> 17:23.240
Oh, dear.

17:23.240 --> 17:25.240
Oh, dear.

17:25.240 --> 17:26.240
Oh, dear.

17:26.240 --> 17:28.240
Oh, oh.

17:28.240 --> 17:43.240
Oh, come on now. Get a hold of your hands and feet.

17:43.240 --> 17:45.240
Oh, man, you're getting water all over us.

17:45.240 --> 17:48.240
I'm getting the water all over everything.

17:48.240 --> 17:50.240
What do we do now?

17:50.240 --> 17:52.240
Find that faucet handle and get it on.

17:52.240 --> 17:54.240
Oh, okay.

17:54.240 --> 17:57.240
Oh, dear.

17:57.240 --> 17:59.240
Oh, oh.

17:59.240 --> 18:00.240
Oh, yeah, I found it.

18:00.240 --> 18:02.240
Well, don't stand there like a statue of liberty.

18:02.240 --> 18:03.240
Get it on.

18:03.240 --> 18:06.240
Oh, dear.

18:06.240 --> 18:07.240
Come on now.

18:07.240 --> 18:08.240
I can't get it off.

18:08.240 --> 18:10.240
Lucy, there's too much pressure.

18:10.240 --> 18:12.240
Oh, you've got to put it the right way.

18:12.240 --> 18:14.240
Oh, I'm not.

18:14.240 --> 18:19.240
Oh, dear.

18:19.240 --> 18:21.240
Oh, no.

18:21.240 --> 18:23.240
Oh, dear.

18:23.240 --> 18:24.240
You're right. There's too much pressure.

18:24.240 --> 18:25.240
Oh, dear.

18:25.240 --> 18:26.240
What do we do now?

18:26.240 --> 18:28.240
Don't ask me. I know from her.

18:28.240 --> 18:29.240
Oh, dear.

18:29.240 --> 18:30.240
I'm not.

18:30.240 --> 18:31.240
Why not?

18:31.240 --> 18:33.240
Well, let's not get nasty.

18:33.240 --> 18:34.240
See?

18:34.240 --> 18:35.240
That water's getting all so high.

18:35.240 --> 18:38.240
You must be standing on the floor, Lucy.

18:38.240 --> 18:39.240
I'm not standing on it.

18:39.240 --> 18:40.240
Come on now.

18:40.240 --> 18:41.240
I'm getting soaked up.

18:41.240 --> 18:43.240
Well, I'm suffocating.

18:43.240 --> 18:44.240
Come on now.

18:44.240 --> 18:45.240
Get the water.

18:45.240 --> 18:47.240
Put your hands over there a minute.

18:47.240 --> 18:49.240
Are you going to suffocate?

18:49.240 --> 18:50.240
Oh.

18:50.240 --> 18:56.240
Oh, dear.

18:56.240 --> 18:59.240
It's got a metal thing over the top of it.

18:59.240 --> 19:01.240
Oh, it's screwed on.

19:01.240 --> 19:02.240
It's screwed on.

19:02.240 --> 19:05.240
Call a plumber.

19:05.240 --> 19:06.240
Call a plumber.

19:06.240 --> 19:07.240
Oh, dear.

19:07.240 --> 19:08.240
Oh, all right.

19:08.240 --> 19:09.240
Come on.

19:09.240 --> 19:10.240
Get out and call the plumber.

19:10.240 --> 19:11.240
What's the matter?

19:11.240 --> 19:13.240
What's the trouble?

19:13.240 --> 19:14.240
The door won't open.

19:14.240 --> 19:15.240
Why not?

19:15.240 --> 19:17.240
I've got too much water in here.

19:17.240 --> 19:18.240
Oh.

19:18.240 --> 19:19.240
Here, help me.

19:19.240 --> 19:20.240
I'll help you.

19:20.240 --> 19:22.240
Come on.

19:22.240 --> 19:24.240
Oh, Lucy.

19:24.240 --> 19:25.240
Oh, dear.

19:25.240 --> 19:29.240
You know, that's the first time I ever saw a shower door that opens in.

19:29.240 --> 19:32.240
What dumb bunny ever...

19:32.240 --> 19:34.240
Oh, dear.

19:34.240 --> 19:36.240
You'll put this door on backwards.

19:36.240 --> 19:37.240
Oh, I'm sorry.

19:37.240 --> 19:38.240
It's so bad.

19:38.240 --> 19:41.240
I guess I just have to watch you every minute.

19:41.240 --> 19:42.240
You can't.

19:42.240 --> 19:45.240
You're too busy forgetting to put washers on faucets.

19:45.240 --> 19:51.240
You know, that wouldn't have mattered if you hadn't been so clumsy and jumped up in that water main.

19:51.240 --> 19:56.240
Well, I wouldn't have broken the water main if you hadn't been too cheap to hire a plumber to come in here and fix it.

19:56.240 --> 19:57.240
All right, all right.

19:57.240 --> 19:58.240
Well, go get somebody.

19:58.240 --> 20:00.240
You ain't gonna get some help.

20:00.240 --> 20:01.240
Where?

20:01.240 --> 20:07.240
Well, maybe somebody will come by the house and save us.

20:07.240 --> 20:08.240
Who?

20:08.240 --> 20:10.240
Some door-to-door frog man?

20:10.240 --> 20:20.240
No, that's me.

20:20.240 --> 20:26.240
Oh, oh.

20:26.240 --> 20:27.240
Hey, you over...

20:27.240 --> 20:28.240
Oh, Lucy.

20:28.240 --> 20:29.240
Lucy.

20:29.240 --> 20:30.240
Oh, you know what?

20:30.240 --> 20:31.240
I just got thought of something.

20:31.240 --> 20:32.240
What?

20:32.240 --> 20:34.240
Did you pay this month's water bill?

20:34.240 --> 20:35.240
Sure I did.

20:35.240 --> 20:41.240
That was a dumb thing to do.

20:41.240 --> 20:43.240
How did I know this was gonna happen?

20:43.240 --> 20:47.240
Oh, well.

20:47.240 --> 20:48.240
I didn't know it was gonna happen.

20:48.240 --> 20:49.240
I know what we're gonna have to do.

20:49.240 --> 20:50.240
What?

20:50.240 --> 20:51.240
We're gonna have to kick this door in.

20:51.240 --> 20:53.240
We're gonna have to break the glass.

20:53.240 --> 20:54.240
Oh, that's a good idea.

20:54.240 --> 20:55.240
OK.

20:55.240 --> 20:57.240
Go ahead, kick it.

20:57.240 --> 20:59.240
Oh, no, you don't.

20:59.240 --> 21:02.240
That's too dangerous.

21:02.240 --> 21:13.240
Not that I'm afraid of cutting myself, but the blood might draw a sharp.

21:13.240 --> 21:17.240
Dear, do you think we could squeeze out through the top?

21:17.240 --> 21:19.240
We might not have to.

21:19.240 --> 21:24.240
In a few minutes, we'll be able to pull it out.

21:24.240 --> 21:27.240
Oh, Lucy.

21:27.240 --> 21:28.240
Hey, girl.

21:28.240 --> 21:29.240
What?

21:29.240 --> 21:32.240
Didn't you say that that cover was held on by screws?

21:32.240 --> 21:33.240
Yeah.

21:33.240 --> 21:35.240
Well, we're gonna have to unscrew it.

21:35.240 --> 21:37.240
We're gonna have to unscrew it?

21:37.240 --> 21:38.240
Yeah.

21:38.240 --> 21:39.240
We can't.

21:39.240 --> 21:40.240
We haven't got a screwdriver.

21:40.240 --> 21:41.240
I have.

21:41.240 --> 21:42.240
You have?

21:42.240 --> 21:43.240
Yeah.

21:43.240 --> 21:49.240
Well, now you tell me.

21:49.240 --> 21:50.240
Oh, boy.

21:50.240 --> 21:55.240
Oh, you think that the people who designed this thing would prepare for the emergency

21:55.240 --> 21:58.240
exit.

21:58.240 --> 22:00.240
I doubt it's in an emergency like this.

22:00.240 --> 22:04.240
Perhaps not very well.

22:04.240 --> 22:06.240
Are you going to go down there and get it out, Lucy?

22:06.240 --> 22:07.240
Yeah.

22:07.240 --> 22:09.240
Come on, you'll get all shriveled if you don't.

22:09.240 --> 22:10.240
Really?

22:10.240 --> 22:11.240
Yeah.

22:11.240 --> 22:14.240
I don't know about you, but I'm not free shrunk.

22:14.240 --> 22:15.240
Get the top off.

22:15.240 --> 22:16.240
Get the top off.

22:16.240 --> 22:17.240
OK.

22:17.240 --> 22:18.240
Are you going?

22:18.240 --> 22:19.240
Yeah.

22:19.240 --> 22:20.240
OK.

22:20.240 --> 22:21.240
Here you go.

22:21.240 --> 22:22.240
Hang on to me.

22:22.240 --> 22:23.240
Hang on to me.

22:23.240 --> 22:24.240
Hang on to me.

22:24.240 --> 22:25.240
That's it.

22:25.240 --> 22:26.240
Go.

22:26.240 --> 22:28.240
You're great.

22:28.240 --> 22:30.240
You're great.

22:30.240 --> 22:32.240
Oh, boy.

22:32.240 --> 22:39.240
Where is Lloyd Bridges when you need him?

22:39.240 --> 22:41.240
Come on.

22:41.240 --> 22:44.240
Get the cover.

22:44.240 --> 22:46.240
The cover.

22:46.240 --> 22:48.240
Hang on, Lucy.

22:48.240 --> 22:50.240
Hang on.

22:50.240 --> 22:52.240
There you go.

22:52.240 --> 22:55.240
Are you getting it, Lucy?

22:55.240 --> 22:56.240
Yeah.

22:56.240 --> 22:57.240
Oh, my God.

22:57.240 --> 22:58.240
Oh, my God.

22:58.240 --> 22:59.240
Oh, my God.

22:59.240 --> 23:00.240
Oh, my God.

23:00.240 --> 23:01.240
Oh, my God.

23:01.240 --> 23:04.240
Want a cup of coffee, Viv?

23:04.240 --> 23:05.240
In a minute.

23:05.240 --> 23:11.240
Lucy, what kind of a house is this?

23:11.240 --> 23:12.240
An hour ago we were awash.

23:12.240 --> 23:15.240
Now I want a drink of water and I've tried every faucet in the place.

23:15.240 --> 23:17.240
Well, I forgot to tell you.

23:17.240 --> 23:21.240
The plumber had to turn the water off while he's fixing the broken handle on the water

23:21.240 --> 23:22.240
main.

23:22.240 --> 23:25.240
Oh, well.

23:25.240 --> 23:30.240
How can you even talk about a drink of water after all we swallowed in that shower?

23:30.240 --> 23:33.240
Well, I can't help it.

23:33.240 --> 23:36.240
Apparently drinking water makes me thirsty.

23:36.240 --> 23:40.240
I'm so sick of that shower I may never wash again.

23:40.240 --> 23:44.240
I'm going to have to learn to lick my paws like a cat.

23:44.240 --> 23:46.240
What plumber did you get, Paisley?

23:46.240 --> 23:47.240
No, Joe.

23:47.240 --> 23:48.240
Joe?

23:48.240 --> 23:52.240
How did you ever get him to come back after all he said?

23:52.240 --> 23:57.240
It took all my diplomacy, all my tax, and all my spending money for the next six months.

23:57.240 --> 24:00.240
I'd feel sorry for you if I weren't so waterlogged.

24:00.240 --> 24:03.240
I guess I shouldn't complain.

24:03.240 --> 24:07.240
You know, all that water could have seeped through the plaster and I would really have

24:07.240 --> 24:08.240
had some expense.

24:08.240 --> 24:10.240
So actually I came out ahead.

24:10.240 --> 24:12.240
Lucy, I want to tell you something.

24:12.240 --> 24:18.240
This is absolutely the last time I slip into my coveralls to be an apprentice on one of

24:18.240 --> 24:19.240
your dreadful little projects.

24:19.240 --> 24:25.240
Now, these are things we're going to look back on and laugh at one day when we're old

24:25.240 --> 24:26.240
and gray.

24:26.240 --> 24:29.240
And from the way things are going, that may be next week.

24:29.240 --> 24:31.240
Oh, soon.

24:31.240 --> 24:37.240
I'll bet we're going to have to plaster the whole ceiling.

24:37.240 --> 24:39.240
Wait, Lucy, absolutely not.

24:39.240 --> 24:40.240
No.

24:40.240 --> 24:46.240
Now, Viv, listen, you have never learned how to plaster and it's all you need to round

24:46.240 --> 25:15.240
you out and you'll be a perfect Mrs. Fixit.

